        {
          "ruleId": "strix-coverage/sql-injection-boolean-based-blind",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "kind": "pass",
          "level": "none",
          "message": {
            "text": "SQL Injection (Boolean-based blind) — Ruled out: /rest/products/search?q parameter\n\nTested boolean-based blind SQLi with payloads `q=juice' AND '1'='1` and `q=juice' AND '1'='2`. Both returned identical 30-byte responses with empty data arrays. No response length differential detected. Time-based SLEEP(2) payload returned 500 error with no delay. The reported vulnerability claim could not be validated. Input appears to be parameterized or escaped at the database layer, preventing SQL injection through the search parameter."
